FUNCTION_BLOCK "SEAM_CLASSIFY"
TITLE =Seam monitor - expected-position tracking
// v2.5 changes vs v2.4:
//   - Fixed v2.4's "R #Alarm" no-op: R is RLO-conditional in STL, and
//     the CLR earlier in the CLEAN PULSE branch (used to clear
//     PreviousSeamWasNone) left RLO=0 going into it, so the reset
//     never actually fired - Alarm stayed latched exactly as before
//     v2.4, confirmed in the field (DB888_PRODUCTION_NEW_FB600_1,
//     2026-09-02: Alarm TRUE all 600/600 records). Added "SET"
//     immediately before the "R", matching the existing
//     SET;R #FirstPulse pattern already in this block. v2.4's stated
//     intent (Alarm self-clears on Clean recovery, no longer latches)
//     is unchanged - this only fixes the instruction that failed to
//     implement it.
//   - NOTE: FB1111 v1.8's DB600 offset shift (+4 bytes, for a claimed
//     "FB600 v2.4 Web_Velocity_Filtered VAR_INPUT") was based on a
//     false premise - that field lives in DB640 (RUN_DATA_DB, added
//     v0.4, owned by FC120 v1.3 for Mega OLED display smoothing) and
//     has never existed in FB600's interface, this version or any
//     other. FB600's VAR section, and therefore DB600's compiled
//     layout, has NOT moved since v2.3. FB1111 needs its own version
//     bump (v1.9) reverting to v1.7's real offsets - see that block's
//     changelog.
//
// v2.4 changes vs v2.3:
//   - Alarm no longer latches. Added "R #Alarm" to the CLEAN PULSE
//     branch (same network that already zeroes BadStreakCount on
//     recovery), so Alarm now self-clears the instant a genuine seam
//     is seen again, instead of sticking until SystemReset or a
//     ReferenceEstablished rising edge (which in practice never came -
//     confirmed across 4 independent 30s production captures,
//     2026-09-02: Alarm latched on the hardcoded 2-consecutive-miss
//     threshold every time, self-healing (BadStreakCount) kept
//     resetting cleanly on every Clean recovery, but Alarm rode out
//     the rest of each capture window still latched). Michou's call:
//     the bottomer's separate No Seam Alarm already stops the machine
//     for a genuine sustained fault, so this Alarm doesn't need to be
//     sticky - it's a live status flag now, not a latch. Trigger
//     condition (2 consecutive StNone misses via PreviousSeamWasNone,
//     independent of MaxBadStreak) is unchanged - only the clear
//     behavior changed. MaxBadStreak-based reacquisition interlock
//     (v2.1, separate network) is untouched.
//
// v2.3 changes vs v2.2:
//   - New diagnostic output ExpWindow_Out: live mirror of the internal
//     #ExpWindow static (the acquired/averaged encoder-count interval
//     between banner pulses - the actual reference pitch the
//     classifier is holding). Added so it can be monitored online and,
//     downstream, used by FB610 to self-clock AGC_Trim while StNone
//     holds level (StNone only edges once per missing-seam streak, so
//     FB610's edge-triggered trim step currently only fires once no
//     matter how long the dead zone continues - encoder-distance
//     clocking off this same pitch value is the planned fix there).
//     Mirrored unconditionally every scan - cheap, and useful to watch
//     move during acquisition too, not just once referenced.
//
// v2.2 changes vs v2.1:
//   - New whole-window spread check during acquisition (AcqWindowMin/Max,
//     SpreadTolerancePct). The existing per-sample check only compares
//     each new interval against the *running average so far* - it
//     catches a single noisy outlier, but not a slow monotonic drift
//     where each new sample individually passes the check while the
//     average quietly chases a still-moving process. Observed case: a
//     mix of ~1000 and ~1120-count intervals during a speed transient
//     averaged into a bogus 1036 ExpWindow that then drifted the
//     classifier off for the next several dozen seams. Acquisition now
//     also requires the min-max spread across the whole accumulated
//     window to stay inside SpreadTolerancePct (tighter than
//     StabilityTolerancePct) before a sample counts toward
//     RequiredStableCount.
//
// v2.1 changes vs v2.0:
//   - New self-healing interlock: after MaxBadStreak consecutive
//     non-Clean classifications (Flick or Missing/Late, in any mix),
//     ReferenceEstablished is cleared automatically, forcing a fresh
//     RequiredStableCount reacquisition against real measured pulses.
//     Without this, a single phase-shifting disturbance (a genuine
//     skipped/extra pulse, a momentary stop/restart, or - as tested -
//     a manual jog via TEST_STIMULUS ForcePulseNow) leaves
//     ExpectedNextPulse permanently offset: Clean/Flick/Missing all
//     advance the schedule by a fixed theoretical ExpWindow step, never
//     by what was actually measured, so nothing ever re-syncs on its
//     own. Previously this required a manual System Reset to recover.
//
// v2.0 changes vs v1.0:
//   - FirstPulse fix: "R #FirstPulse" now preceded by SET, not CLR
//     (R/S are conditional coils - CLR forced RLO=0 so it never fired).
//   - Classification (StNone/StClean/StFlick) and the missing-seam
//     Alarm now run whenever Machine_Run=TRUE, independent of
//     Auto_Mode. Auto switch no longer gates the classify/tolerance/
//     missing-seam networks - it only remains relevant to whatever
//     FB610 does with ReferenceEstablished + Auto_Mode to close the
//     AGC loop, outside this block.
//   - Expected-position tracking now starts on the rising edge of
//     ReferenceEstablished, not on the rising edge of Auto_Mode -
//     so live feedback runs the moment reference latches, in Manual.
//   - New interlock: ReferenceEstablished (and StableCount/
//     ReferenceSum) are forced to zero on:
//       a) falling edge of Auto_Mode (operator switches Auto off)
//       b) PotMoved = TRUE (operator is touching the pot)
//     Reacquisition (RequiredStableCount consecutive clean intervals)
//     is required again before Reference OK can re-latch.
//   - Bootstrap acquisition network no longer requires Auto_Mode=FALSE
//     to run - only requires ReferenceEstablished=FALSE. This lets it
//     resume automatically the instant (a) or (b) above clears the bit,
//     without waiting for the operator to also flip the Auto switch.
//   - RequiredStableCount default raised 5 -> 10.
//
// INTEGRATION NOTE:
//   PotMoved must be supplied by FB610 / the Mega side - it has no
//   direct visibility of the pot (point B goes straight to Mega A6).
//   Wire it as: TRUE while |PotValue - LastPotValue| exceeds your
//   deadband, FALSE once settled. Level signal is fine - as long as
//   it's TRUE, this block keeps clearing ReferenceEstablished, which
//   is exactly "if the operator keeps turning the pot: no Reference OK."
VERSION : 2.5


VAR_INPUT
  EncoderSnapshot : DINT ;	// Captured by OB40
  LiveEncoderCount : DINT ;	// Current FM350-2 encoder count
  BannerEventCount : DINT ;	// Incremented by OB40
  Machine_Run : BOOL ;	
  Auto_Mode : BOOL ;	
  SystemReset : BOOL ;	
  PotMoved : BOOL ;	// NEW - from FB610: pot wiper moved beyond deadband
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
  StNone : BOOL ;	
  StClean : BOOL ;	
  StFlick : BOOL ;	
  Alarm : BOOL ;	
  ReferenceEstablished : BOOL ;	// "Reference OK" - gates Auto availability
  ExpWindow_Out : DINT ;	// NEW v2.3 - live mirror of #ExpWindow, the acquired reference pitch (encoder co
END_VAR
VAR
  LastBannerEventCount : DINT ;	
  LastPulseEncoder : DINT ;	
  FirstPulse : BOOL  := TRUE;	// Reference acquisi
  ExpWindow : DINT  := L#5000;	
  ReferenceSum : DINT ;	
  StableCount : INT ;	
  RequiredStableCount : INT  := 10;	// was 5
  StabilityTolerancePct : INT  := 15;	// Expected seam tra
  SpreadTolerancePct : INT  := 5;	// NEW v2.2 - max whole-window spread during acquisition (tighter than StabilityT
  AcqWindowMin : DINT ;	// NEW v2.2 - min PulseDelta seen in current acquisition attempt
  AcqWindowMax : DINT ;	// NEW v2.2 - max PulseDelta seen in current acquisition attempt
  ExpectedNextPulse : DINT ;	
  ExpectedPositionValid : BOOL ;	
  EarlyTolerancePct : INT  := 30;	
  LateTolerancePct : INT  := 30;	
  PreviousSeamWasNone : BOOL ;	// Internal state:
// 0 = None
// 1 = Clean
// 2 = Flick
// 3 = Idle / no classification
  StateCode : INT  := 3;	// Edge memories
//===
  RefEstMem : BOOL ;	// NEW - edge memory, ReferenceEstablished rising edge
  AutoOffMem : BOOL ;	// NEW - edge memory, Auto_Mode falling edge
  BadStreakCount : INT ;	// v2.1 - consecutive non-Clean classifications
  MaxBadStreak : INT  := 5;	// v2.1 - clears Reference OK once reached
  SystemResetMem : BOOL ;	
END_VAR
VAR_TEMP
  NewEventCount : DINT ;	
  PulseDelta : DINT ;	
  CandidateAverage : DINT ;	
  StableCountD : DINT ;	
  Difference : DINT ;	
  StabilityBand : DINT ;	
  SpreadBand : DINT ;	// NEW v2.2 - allowed spread = CandidateAverage * SpreadTolerancePct / 100
  ProspectiveMin : DINT ;	// NEW v2.2 - window min if current PulseDelta is accepted
  ProspectiveMax : DINT ;	// NEW v2.2 - window max if current PulseDelta is accepted
  Spread : DINT ;	// NEW v2.2 - ProspectiveMax - ProspectiveMin
  EarlyTolerance : DINT ;	
  LateTolerance : DINT ;	
  EarliestPosition : DINT ;	
  LatestPosition : DINT ;	
END_VAR
BEGIN
NETWORK
TITLE =System reset - complete re-acquisition

      A     #SystemReset; 
      FP    #SystemResetMem; 
      JCN   R001; 

      L     #BannerEventCount; // Synchronize to the current OB40 event count.
      T     #LastBannerEventCount; // Old Banner events are not replayed after reset.
//;
      L     0; 
      T     #LastPulseEncoder; 
      T     "SEAM_CLASSIFY_DB".EncoderSnapshot; 
      T     "SEAM_CLASSIFY_DB".LiveEncoderCount; 
      T     "SEAM_CLASSIFY_DB".BannerEventCount; 
      T     "SEAM_CLASSIFY_DB".LastBannerEventCount; 
//;
      T     #ReferenceSum; 
      T     #StableCount; 
      T     #ExpectedNextPulse; 
      T     #ExpWindow; 

      SET   ; 
      =     #FirstPulse; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #ReferenceEstablished; 
      =     #ExpectedPositionValid; 
      =     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 
      =     #Alarm; 
//;
      L     3; 
      T     #StateCode; 
//;
      L     0; 
      T     #BadStreakCount; 

R001: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Detect number of new OB40 Banner events

      L     #BannerEventCount; 
      L     #LastBannerEventCount; 
      -D    ; 
      T     #NewEventCount; 
//;
      L     #NewEventCount; // Counter was reset or wrapped unexpectedly.
      L     0; 
      >=D   ; 
      JC    E001; 

      L     #BannerEventCount; 
      T     #LastBannerEventCount; 
//;
      L     0; 
      T     #NewEventCount; 

E001: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =First Banner pulse establishes encoder origin

      L     #NewEventCount; 
      L     0; 
      <=D   ; 
      JC    F001; 

      A     #FirstPulse; 
      JCN   F001; 

      L     #EncoderSnapshot; 
      T     #LastPulseEncoder; 
//;
      L     #BannerEventCount; 
      T     #LastBannerEventCount; 
//;
      L     0; 
      T     #NewEventCount; 

      SET   ; 
      R     #FirstPulse; 

F001: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Lose Reference OK on Auto-mode falling edge

      A     #Auto_Mode; 
      FN    #AutoOffMem; 
      JCN   L010; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #ReferenceEstablished; 
      =     #ExpectedPositionValid; 
//;
      L     0; 
      T     #StableCount; 
      T     #ReferenceSum; 

L010: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Lose Reference OK on pot movement

      A     #PotMoved; 
      JCN   L020; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #ReferenceEstablished; 
      =     #ExpectedPositionValid; 
//;
      L     0; 
      T     #StableCount; 
      T     #ReferenceSum; 

L020: NOP   0; 


NETWORK
TITLE =Classifications
//Lose Reference OK after repeated bad classifications (self-healing resync)
      L     #BadStreakCount; 
      L     #MaxBadStreak; 
      <I    ; 
      JC    L030; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #ReferenceEstablished; 
      =     #ExpectedPositionValid; 
//;
      L     0; 
      T     #StableCount; 
      T     #ReferenceSum; 
      T     #BadStreakCount; 

L030: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Acquisition 
//Acquisition - stability-gated reference building (any switch position)
      L     #NewEventCount; 
      L     0; 
      <=D   ; 
      JC    M099; 

      A     #Machine_Run; 
      JCN   M099; 

      A     #ReferenceEstablished; 
      JC    M099; 

      L     #NewEventCount; // More than one interrupt occurred between two OB1 scans.
      L     1; // Only the final encoder snapshot remains available.
      >D    ; 
      JC    M080; 
//;
      L     #EncoderSnapshot; // Calculate pulse-to-pulse encoder distance.
      L     #LastPulseEncoder; 
      -D    ; 
      T     #PulseDelta; 
//;
      L     #PulseDelta; // Reject zero or reverse movement.
      L     0; 
      >D    ; 
      JC    M010; 

      JU    M080; 

M010: L     #StableCount; // First usable interval initializes the candidate average
      L     0; 
      >I    ; 
      JC    M020; 

      L     #PulseDelta; 
      T     #ReferenceSum; 
//;
      L     1; 
      T     #StableCount; 
//;
      L     #PulseDelta; 
      T     #AcqWindowMin; 
      T     #AcqWindowMax; 
//;
      L     1; 
      T     #StateCode; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 

      JU    M070; 

M020: L     #StableCount; // Calculate candidate running average
      ITD   ; 
      T     #StableCountD; 

      L     #ReferenceSum; 
      L     #StableCountD; 
      /D    ; 
      T     #CandidateAverage; 
//;
      L     #PulseDelta; // Difference = PulseDelta - CandidateAverage
      L     #CandidateAverage; 
      -D    ; 
      T     #Difference; 
//;
      L     #Difference; // Absolute value of Difference
      L     0; 
      >=D   ; 
      JC    M030; 

      L     0; 
      L     #Difference; 
      -D    ; 
      T     #Difference; 

M030: L     #CandidateAverage; // Stability tolerance band (per-sample outlier rejection)
      L     #StabilityTolerancePct; 
      ITD   ; 
      *D    ; 
      L     L#100; 
      /D    ; 
      T     #StabilityBand; 
//;
      L     #StabilityBand; // Minimum tolerance is one encoder count.
      L     1; 
      >=D   ; 
      JC    M032; 

      L     1; 
      T     #StabilityBand; 

M032: L     #CandidateAverage; // Spread tolerance band (whole-window settling check
      L     #SpreadTolerancePct; 
      ITD   ; 
      *D    ; 
      L     L#100; 
      /D    ; 
      T     #SpreadBand; 
//;
      L     #SpreadBand; 
      L     1; 
      >=D   ; 
      JC    M034; 

      L     1; 
      T     #SpreadBand; 

M034: L     #AcqWindowMin; // Prospective window minimum if this sample were accepted
      L     #PulseDelta; 
      <D    ; 
      JC    M035; 

      L     #PulseDelta; 
      T     #ProspectiveMin; 

      JU    M036; 

M035: L     #AcqWindowMin; 
      T     #ProspectiveMin; 

M036: L     #AcqWindowMax; // Prospective window maximum if this sample were accepted
      L     #PulseDelta; 
      >D    ; 
      JC    M037; 

      L     #PulseDelta; 
      T     #ProspectiveMax; 

      JU    M040; 

M037: L     #AcqWindowMax; 
      T     #ProspectiveMax; 

M040: L     #Difference; // Compare new interval against running average AND whole-window spread
      L     #StabilityBand; 
      >D    ; 
      JC    M045; 

      L     #ProspectiveMax; 
      L     #ProspectiveMin; 
      -D    ; 
      T     #Spread; 
//;
      L     #Spread; 
      L     #SpreadBand; 
      <=D   ; 
      JC    M050; 

M045: L     #PulseDelta; // Unstable interval, begin a new acquisition show Flick.
      T     #ReferenceSum; 
//;
      L     1; 
      T     #StableCount; 
//;
      L     #PulseDelta; 
      T     #AcqWindowMin; 
      T     #AcqWindowMax; 
//;
      L     2; 
      T     #StateCode; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 

      JU    M070; 

M050: L     #ReferenceSum; // Stable interval - add it to the running sum, commit the window
      L     #PulseDelta; 
      +D    ; 
      T     #ReferenceSum; 
//;
      L     #StableCount; 
      L     1; 
      +I    ; 
      T     #StableCount; 
//;
      L     #ProspectiveMin; 
      T     #AcqWindowMin; 
//;
      L     #ProspectiveMax; 
      T     #AcqWindowMax; 
//;
      L     1; 
      T     #StateCode; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 

      L     #StableCount; // Is the required stable count reached?
      L     #RequiredStableCount; 
      <I    ; 
      JC    M070; 

      L     #StableCount; // Calculate final averaged reference.
      ITD   ; 
      T     #StableCountD; 
//;
      L     #ReferenceSum; 
      L     #StableCountD; 
      /D    ; 
      T     #ExpWindow; 

      SET   ; 
      =     #ReferenceEstablished; 

      JU    M070; 

M080: L     0; // Invalid reference sample - noisy read, show Flick
      T     #ReferenceSum; 
      T     #StableCount; 

      L     2; 
      T     #StateCode; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 

M070: L     #EncoderSnapshot; // Store the latest pulse position
      T     #LastPulseEncoder; 

      L     #BannerEventCount; 
      T     #LastBannerEventCount; 

      L     0; 
      T     #NewEventCount; // Event fully consumed

M099: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Reference established - start expected-position sequence

      A     #ReferenceEstablished; 
      FP    #RefEstMem; 
      JCN   A099; 

      L     3; 
      T     #StateCode; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 
      =     #Alarm; 
//;
      L     #LastPulseEncoder; // Start one reference pitch after the most recenpulse.
      L     #ExpWindow; 
      +D    ; 
      T     #ExpectedNextPulse; 

      SET   ; 
      =     #ExpectedPositionValid; 

A099: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Calculate early and late tolerance positions

      A     #Machine_Run; 
      JCN   T099; 

      A     #ReferenceEstablished; 
      JCN   T099; 

      A     #ExpectedPositionValid; 
      JCN   T099; 

      L     #ExpWindow; // Early tolerance
      L     #EarlyTolerancePct; 
      ITD   ; 
      *D    ; 
      L     L#100; 
      /D    ; 
      T     #EarlyTolerance; 
//;
      L     #ExpWindow; // Late tolerance
      L     #LateTolerancePct; 
      ITD   ; 
      *D    ; 
      L     L#100; 
      /D    ; 
      T     #LateTolerance; 
//;
      L     #ExpectedNextPulse; 
      L     #EarlyTolerance; 
      -D    ; 
      T     #EarliestPosition; 
//;
      L     #ExpectedNextPulse; 
      L     #LateTolerance; 
      +D    ; 
      T     #LatestPosition; 

T099: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Classify new Banner event (any switch position, once referenced)

      L     #NewEventCount; 
      L     0; 
      <=D   ; 
      JC    C099; 

      A     #Machine_Run; 
      JCN   C090; 
//;
      A     #ReferenceEstablished; 
      JCN   C090; 
//;
      A     #ExpectedPositionValid; 
      JCN   C090; 

      L     #NewEventCount; // More than one pulse between OB1 scans is flicking.
      L     1; 
      >D    ; 
      JC    C060; 

      L     #EncoderSnapshot; // Pulse before the valid window is a flick.
      L     #EarliestPosition; 
      <D    ; 
      JC    C060; 

      L     #EncoderSnapshot; // Pulse after the late limit means the expected seam was missed.
      L     #LatestPosition; 
      >D    ; 
      JC    C070; 

      L     1; // CLEAN PULS
      T     #StateCode; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 

      L     0; 
      T     #BadStreakCount; 
      SET   ; // required - R is RLO-conditional and CLR above left RLO=0,
// which made the unguarded R #Alarm below a silent no-op
// (same pattern as SET;R #FirstPulse elsewhere in this block)
      R     #Alarm; // v2.5 - self-clear on Clean recovery; downstream No Seam
// Alarm already handles the stop-worthy case, so Alarm here
// no longer needs to latch pending SystemReset/reacquisition.
//;
      L     #ExpectedNextPulse; // Advance from the theoretical expected position,
      L     #ExpWindow; // not from the actual measured pulse position.
      +D    ; 
      T     #ExpectedNextPulse; 

      JU    C090; 

C060: L     2; // FLICK PULSE
      T     #StateCode; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 

      L     #BadStreakCount; // Do not advance ExpectedNextPulse.
      L     1; // The genuine seam pulse is still expected.
      +I    ; 
      T     #BadStreakCount; 

      JU    C090; 

C070: L     0; // LATE PULSE - expected seam is considered missing
      T     #StateCode; 
//;
      L     #BadStreakCount; 
      L     1; 
      +I    ; 
      T     #BadStreakCount; 
//;
      A     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 
      JCN   C075; 

      SET   ; 
      =     #Alarm; 

      JU    C080; 

C075: SET   ; 
      =     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 

C080: L     #ExpectedNextPulse; // Advance exactly one theoretical seam pitch.
      L     #ExpWindow; 
      +D    ; 
      T     #ExpectedNextPulse; 

C090: L     #EncoderSnapshot; // Consume captured OB40 events
      T     #LastPulseEncoder; 
//;
      L     #BannerEventCount; 
      T     #LastBannerEventCount; 

C099: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Detect missing Banner seam (any switch position, once referenced

      A     #Machine_Run; 
      JCN   N099; 

      A     #ReferenceEstablished; 
      JCN   N099; 

      A     #ExpectedPositionValid; 
      JCN   N099; 

      L     #NewEventCount; // An OB40 event is waiting to be processed.
      L     0; // Let the event-classification network handle it.
      >D    ; 
      JC    N099; 

      L     #LiveEncoderCount; // Has the encoder passed the late limit?
      L     #LatestPosition; 
      <=D   ; 
      JC    N099; 

      L     0; // MISSING SEAM
      T     #StateCode; 
//;
      L     #BadStreakCount; 
      L     1; 
      +I    ; 
      T     #BadStreakCount; 
//;
      A     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 
      JCN   N010; 

      SET   ; 
      =     #Alarm; 

      JU    N020; 

N010: SET   ; 
      =     #PreviousSeamWasNone; 

N020: L     #ExpectedNextPulse; // Advance by one expected pitch.
      L     #ExpWindow; 
      +D    ; 
      T     #ExpectedNextPulse; 

N099: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Machine stopped - drain unused Banner events

      AN    #Machine_Run; 
      JCN   S099; 

      L     #BannerEventCount; 
      T     #LastBannerEventCount; 

S099: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Decode mutually-exclusive state outputs

      CLR   ; 
      =     #StNone; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #StClean; 

      CLR   ; 
      =     #StFlick; 

      L     #StateCode; 
      L     0; 
      ==I   ; 
      JCN   D010; 

      SET   ; 
      =     #StNone; 

      JU    D099; 

D010: L     #StateCode; 
      L     1; 
      ==I   ; 
      JCN   D020; 

      SET   ; 
      =     #StClean; 

      JU    D099; 

D020: L     #StateCode; 
      L     2; 
      ==I   ; 
      JCN   D099; 

      SET   ; 
      =     #StFlick; 

D099: NOP   0; 
NETWORK
TITLE =Mirror ExpWindow to diagnostic output (NEW v2.3)

      L     #ExpWindow; 
      T     #ExpWindow_Out; 


NETWORK
TITLE =Green Lamp Reset

      AN    #Machine_Run; 
      L     S5T#5S; 
      SD    T    105; 
//;
      A     T    105; 
      R     #StClean; // To Turn OFF the Green Led !
END_FUNCTION_BLOCK

